# Snap-On Clothing — asset library locations.
#
# This is the store the Setup tab reads and writes. You can also manage it by
# hand: rename this file to "path.txt" (same folder, beside the snap_on_clothing
# package) and set your two folders below. Blank lines and lines starting with
# "#" are ignored. An installer upgrade never overwrites your path.txt.
#
#   local  = your working library. The tool scans ONLY this folder.
#   remote = a shared master library (studio server / drive). It is never scanned;
#            the Setup tab's "Sync from remote" button pulls new and changed
#            assets down from here into your local folder (it never deletes).
#
# When "local" is unset, the tool falls back to its built-in default library.
#
# Examples (delete these and set your own):

# Windows — local drive + shared UNC master:
# local  = D:/clothing_library
# remote = //studio-nas/projects/genhuman/clothing

# macOS / Linux — local disk + mounted share:
# local  = /Users/me/clothing_library
# remote = /Volumes/clothing/assets
